  "name": "Reisado and guerreiro (Northeastern Epiphany folguedo)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Epiphany-cycle folk drama of the Brazilian Northeast in which a troupe led by a mestre and contramestre, with kings, a queen, Mateus clowns and sword-bearing figures, dances and sings embassies and short scenes from Christmas to the Dia de Reis; the reisados of the Cariri region of Ceará around Juazeiro do Norte are among the best known. The guerreiro of Alagoas grew out of the reisado in the twentieth century, its dancers wearing tall mirrored headdresses. The accompaniment is a small band of accordion or fifes with zabumba and other percussion; a generic membrane-drum card stands in for the zabumba.",
